\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
Does every type $II_{1}$ factor with separable predual have one bounded operator x with $W*(x)=M$, equivalently two self-adjoint von Neumann generators? This asks for von Neumann generation and makes no norm-closed C*-generation assertion.

\subsection{Short English statement}
Does every type $II_{1}$ factor with separable predual have one bounded operator x with $W*(x)=M$, equivalently two self-adjoint von Neumann generators? This asks for von Neumann generation and makes no norm-closed C*-generation assertion.

\subsection{Sources}
\begin{itemize}
\item[S1] OpenAI, manuscript citation page. Source of the formulation motivating this local problem.
\url{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/Relative-generation-and-the-generator-problem-for-finite-factors-September-23-2026/README.md}.
\end{itemize}

